quran[7]{c,v,t}:
  9,80,"(It does not matter) whether you seek forgiveness for them or do not seek forgiveness for them, even if you seek forgiveness for them seventy times (out of your kindness and mercy), Allah shall never forgive them. That is because they rejected Allah and His Messenger (blessings and peace be upon him). And Allah does not guide the transgressing people."
  9,81,"(These hypocrites are) those who stayed behind (from participating in the expedition to Tabuk with the Prophet (blessings and peace be upon him) and were happy for their sitting back, opposing (the command of) Allah’s Messenger (blessings and peace be upon him), and they hated to strive with their possessions and their persons for the cause of Allah. And they said: ‘Do not go out (with the Prophet (blessings and peace be upon him) in this heat.’ Say: ‘The Fire of Hell is much hotter if they could understand.’"
  9,82,So let them laugh a little; they will weep much as a reward for what they used to earn.
  9,83,"If Allah brings you back (from the battlefront of Tabuk) to a group of them and they seek your permission to go forth (for any further expeditions), say (to them): ‘By no means shall you ever go forth with me, and by no means shall you ever fight an enemy with me. You were pleased to sit back the first time (i.e. the most crucial moment); therefore, sit (this time again) with those who remain behind.’"
  9,84,"And do not ever offer the (funeral) prayers for any of their dead, nor stand by their grave. Indeed, they defied Allah and His Messenger (blessings and peace be upon him) and died rebellious."
  9,85,And let neither their possessions nor their children impress you. Allah desires only to punish them through these (things) in this world and that their souls may depart while they are disbelievers.
  9,86,"And when a (Qur’anic) Chapter is revealed, (saying:) ‘Believe in Allah and struggle along with His Messenger (blessings and peace be upon him),’ the affluent among them ask you for leave and say: ‘Let us remain with those who are sitting back (among the women and children).’"
